WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.130
Belo Horizonte, in south-east Brazil.

2
00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:06.330
A city of about 2.5 million people.

3
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:10.990
In 1993, a city law made
access to food a right.

4
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.370
It set up a food secretariat.

5
00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:16.810
Its food system has about 20 programmes.

6
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.130
Researchers call it a world pioneer.

7
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:21.870
Its ideas were copied across Brazil.

8
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.170
But a law can't fill a plate.

9
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:26.030
So what did the city do?

10
00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.590
Hand out food parcels?

11
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:28.980
Ban food exports?

12
00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:33.010
In this mission, you'll test what
makes a food supply sustainable:

13
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:36.170
for the land, the economy and people.

14
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.200
Then you'll take the city's scheme apart,

15
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:41.990
programme by programme, and
judge how well it worked.

16
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:46.920
Your mission: find out how Belo
Horizonte made the right to food real.
